According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global IGBT Power Device Market was valued at USD 10.1 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 19.2 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 9.8% during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is propelled by intensified adoption of electric mobility, renewable energy conversion, and industrial automation.
An IGBT (Insulated Gate Bipolar Transistor) power device is a semiconductor switch that marries the gate drive simplicity of MOSFETs with the high current capability of bipolar transistors. It underpins medium to high power applications such as motor drives, grid connected inverters for solar and wind farms, traction converters for rail and electric vehicles, and industrial power supplies. Product families include compact discrete IGBTs, high density modular IGBTs, and press pack IGBTs that deliver robustness in harsh environments like rail traction and aerospace systems.
